# Read by /etc/init.d/S01seedrng. seedrng keeps its seed in
# /var/lib/seedrng by default, which is on the read-only root, so it
# failed on every boot. The data partition is mounted only later (S41),
# so there is no persistent place this early: keep the seed on tmpfs.
# Losing it at every reboot costs little: the kernel seeds its RNG on its
# own (jitter entropy), and nothing in the kiosk does cryptography.
SEEDRNG_ARGS="--seed-dir=/run/seedrng"
